      "source_summary": {
        "content": "Analysis shows Line 7 disruptions caused 50,000 lost passenger journeys last month, directly justifying the upgrade. No additional data needed. Given the critical loss of 50,000 passenger journeys on Line 7, I request manual approval for the signaling upgrade. This is urgent because automated tools can't complete budget approval or contractor signing due to mismatched contract types and missing financial parameters. To proceed with passenger communications for the Line 7 closure, provide: 1. Service alert parameters—severity (info/minor/major/severe), title, detailed message with guidance, exa ... [middle omitted] ...  end time. 2. Alternative route O-D pairs (origin/destination) and notification parameters (channel, audience, message). Note: Bulk refunds for 50,000 affected journeys are critical but require unavailable inputs (incidentId, affectedTrips, etc.); recommend manual processing.",
        "role": "agent"
      }
    },
